.TH SCOPEBRIDGE-GUI 1 "September 2026" "scopebridge" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
scopebridge-gui, scopebridge \- graphical front end for a Rigol DS1000Z-E oscilloscope
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B scopebridge
.RB [ \-\-usb
.IR DEVICE " | " \fB\-\-lan\fR " " HOST " | " \fB\-\-sim\fR ]
.RB [ \-\-port
.IR N ]
.br
.B scopebridge
.B \-\-host
.I HOST
.RB [ \-\-port
.IR N ]
.br
.B scopebridge-gui
.RB [ \-\-host
.IR HOST ]
.RB [ \-\-port
.IR N ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B scopebridge-gui
shows the scope's waveforms live and has its common controls: channels,
timebase, edge, pulse and slope triggers, measurements (recordable to
CSV), cursors, math and FFT (by the scope or on the PC), an XY
display, the pass/fail test, reference waveforms, and decoding of UART,
I2C and SPI traffic. A capture of the whole acquisition memory can be
zoomed and panned through. Setups, screenshots and CSV exports are saved
to files.
.PP
It is a client of
.BR scopebridge-server (1),
which it connects to on
.IR HOST : N
(default 127.0.0.1:5026).
.B scopebridge
starts the server and the GUI together and stops the server when the GUI
closes; without
.BR \-\-usb ,
.B \-\-lan
or
.B \-\-sim
it finds the scope on USB. If a server is already listening on the port
(for example the systemd service), it just starts the GUI.
With
.B \-\-host
it starts only the GUI, for a server running on another computer (such as
a Raspberry Pi the scope is connected to, running
.BR "scopebridge-server \-\-listen 0.0.0.0" ).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-usb " DEVICE\fR, " \-\-lan " HOST\fR, " \-\-sim
.RB ( scopebridge
only) where the scope is, as for
.BR scopebridge-server (1).
.TP
.BI \-\-host " HOST"
The server's computer; default 127.0.0.1.
.TP
.BI \-\-port " N"
The server's port.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I @DOCDIR@/MANUAL.md
The user manual, with screenshots of every panel.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR scopebridge-server (1),
.BR scopebridge-term (1),
.BR scopebridge-run (1)
